const char *sub_180179F30()
{
  return "Specifies shadows for boxes, or inset shadows/glows.  The shadow shape will match the border box for the panel,"
         "so use border-radius to affect rounding.  Syntax takes optional shape 'inset', 'fill', or 'hollow', then color,"
         " horizontal offset pixels, vertical offset pixels, blur radius pixels, and spread distance in pixels. Inset mea"
         "ns the shadow is an inner shadow/glow, fill is a a shadow behind the entire box, hollow means clipping it to ou"
         "tside the border area only (before offset). A negative blur radius will give a hard-edged look to the shadow, e"
         "ffectively a rounded outline of the same size as the blur.<br><br><b>Examples:</b><pre>box-shadow: #ffffff80 4p"
         "x 4px 8px 0px; // outer, filled\n"
         "box-shadow: hollow #ffffff80 4px 4px 8px 0px; // outer, hollow\n"
         "box-shadow: inset #333333b0 0px 0px 8px 12px; // inner</pre>";
}

